      <div type="clause" n="22.1a">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 22.1a</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="22.1a" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="324" ed="#liebermann"/>And ofgá man anfealde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IICn_22-1a.lnote.oe.11"/> lade mid<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#IICn_22-1a.lnote.oe.12"/> anfealdan foraðe ⁊ þryfealde lade mid þryfealdan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#IICn_22-1a.lnote.oe.13-2"/> foraðe.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="22.1a" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="324" ed="#liebermann"/>Ofga mán anfealde láde mid anfealde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_22-1a.lnote.oe.5"/> foraðe ⁊ ðrifealde lade mid ðrifealdan foraðe.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="22.1a" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="324" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ ofga man anfealdne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_22-1a.lnote.oe.5-2"/> lade mid<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IICn_22-1a.lnote.oe.7"/> þryfealde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_22-1a.lnote.oe.5-2"/> foraðe.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="22.1a" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="325" ed="#liebermann"/>Et inducatur simplex láda<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#IICn_22-1a.lnote.oe.13"/> (id<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#IICn_22-1a.lnote.oe.14"/> est purgatio) simplici preiuramento, triplex lada triplici<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#IICn_22-1a.lnote.oe.15"/> preiuramento.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="22.1a" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="325" ed="#liebermann"/>Qui autem conquirere<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#IICn_22-1a.lnote.oe.15-2"/> debet simplicem<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#IICn_22-1a.lnote.oe.14-2"/> purgationem, simplici sacramento hoc faciat, hoc est accipiat duos, et sit ipse tertius et sic iurando conquirat.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#IICn_22-1a.lnote.oe.16"/> Triplex<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="*" target="#IICn_22-1a.lnote.oe.star-2"/> uero<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#IICn_22-1a.lnote.oe.17"/> iuramentum sic conquiratur: accipiat quinque et sit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#IICn_22-1a.lnote.oe.18"/> ipse sextus et sic iurando adquirat triplex iudicium aut triplex iuramentum.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#IICn_22-1a.lnote.oe.19"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="22.1a" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="325" ed="#liebermann"/>Simplexque purgatio attingatur simplici preiuramento et triplex triplici.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="22.1a" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="184" ed="#robertson"/>Ofga mán anfealde láde mid anfealde foraðe ⁊ ðrifealde lade<ptr type="editorNote" n="14" target="#IICn_22-1a.robnote.fn.14"/> mid ðrifealdan foraðe.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="264" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And ofga man anfealde lade mid anfealdan foraðe and þryfealde lade mid þryfealdan foraðe.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="325" ed="#liebermann"/>Und<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_22-1a.lnote.de.1"/> man [Kläger<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_22-1a.lnote.de.2"/>] erzwinge einfache Reinigung durch einfachen Klageeid<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_22-1a.lnote.de.3"/> und dreifache Reinigung durch dreifachen Klageeid.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And let [the plaintiff] compel the single clearing by a single fore-oath, and the threefold clearing by a threefold fore-oath.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="185" ed="#robertson"/>In cases where a simple oath of exculpation is involved, the case shall be begun with a simple oath of accusation<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_22-1a.robnote.n.1"/>, but where a triple oath of exculpation is involved, it shall be begun with a triple oath of accusation<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IICn_22-1a.robnote.n.2"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="465" ed="#whitelock"/>And a simple process of exculpation is to be set on foot by a simple preliminary oath, and a three-fold process of exculpation by a three-fold preliminary oath.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="265" ed="#rabin-doml"/>and a case requiring the threefold oath of exculpation is to be initiated with a threefold oath of accusation.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:IICn_30-3a">II Cn 30.3a</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">A skips a line (from ‘mid anfealdan’ to ‘þryfealde’).; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 325, October 2026 (MS Cons); AV: corrected against Rabin p. 264, October 2026 (was “And a case requiring the simple oath of exculpation is to be initiated with a simple oath of accusation,”, now “∅”)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">mid . . . lade: omitted A</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_22-1a.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">325</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">semplex <hi rend="italic">Hr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">semplex Hr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_22-1a.lnote.oe.star" n="*" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">325</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">folgt Glosse</hi> Preiuramentum <hi rend="italic">Hk; s. u.:</hi> ‘Rechtsbücher 12. Jhs.’</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">followed by the gloss Preiuramentum Hk; see below: ‘Rechtsbücher 12. Jhs.’</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_22-1a.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">324</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_22-1a.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">325</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">lada — triplex <hi rend="italic">überspringt K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lada — triplex skipped by K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_22-1a.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">325</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">i. p. <hi rend="italic">fehlt Hn</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">i. p. lacking in Hn</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_22-1a.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">325</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_22-1a.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">324</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-dne <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-dne Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_22-1a.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">324</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">mid — lade <hi rend="italic">fehlt Ld</hi> [<hi rend="italic">vgl. A</hi>]</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">mid — lade lacking in Ld [cf. A]</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_22-1a.lnote.oe.13-2" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">324</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-lde <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-lde Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_22-1a.lnote.oe.5-2" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">324</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_22-1a.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">324</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Zeile übersprungen</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">line skipped</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_22-1a.lnote.oe.15-2" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">325</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">d. c. <hi rend="italic">H</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">d. c. H</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_22-1a.lnote.oe.14-2" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">325</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">später am Rande Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">later in the margin Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_22-1a.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">325</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">perq. <hi rend="italic">Lb S</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">perq. Lb S</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_22-1a.lnote.oe.star-2" n="*" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">325</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vgl. unten</hi> 30, 3<hi rend="italic">a</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cf. below 30, 3a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_22-1a.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">325</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">iudicium uel <hi rend="italic">fügt zu Lb S</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">iudicium uel added by Lb S</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_22-1a.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">325</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_22-1a.lnote.oe.19" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">325</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sacram. <hi rend="italic">Lb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sacram. Lb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_22-1a.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">205</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Wiederholt durch Hn 64, 9</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Repeated by Hn 64, 9</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_22-1a.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">205</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Über <hi rend="italic">ofgan</hi> (nicht ‘trete an’, als gäbe es Voreid des Beklagten; Schmid 579) <hi rend="italic">s</hi>. II As 23, 2¹</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">On <hi rend="italic">ofgan</hi> (not ‘come forward’, as if there were a preliminary oath by the defendant; Schmid 579) <hi rend="italic">see</hi> II As 23, 2¹</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_22-1a.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">205</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Klageeid 11. 13b. c. Aus Inst schöpft hier Ps Cn for 11</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Klageeid 11. 13b. c. Ps Cn for 11 draws on Inst here</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_22-1a.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">355</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">forað</hi> means lit. ‘preliminary oath,’ <hi rend="italic">i.e.</hi> the oath sworn by the accuser in beginning his action.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_22-1a.robnote.n.2" n="2" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">355</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Inst. explains more fully the difference between a simple oath of accusation and a triple one: <hi rend="italic">simplici sacramento…hoc est accipiat duos et sit ipse tertius…triplex…accipiat quinque et sit ipse sextus</hi>.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_22-1a.robnote.fn.14" n="14" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">184</biblScope></bibl><label>lade</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">mid anf….lade</hi> om. A, Ld.</seg></note>
